# A real attack on an event platform with email marketing (2026). A new
# account signs up with Google, creates a page and a crew (its tenant),
# starts a paid-plan trial with a foreign debit card in someone else's name,
# turns on email marketing and imports four addresses of its own, one per
# big mailbox provider: an inbox placement probe, the usual step before a
# spam or phishing run. With the packs acting, the trial is put on the free
# plan's quotas for review, and the account is quarantined at the contact
# import, before any mail leaves. The same person comes back with a new
# account and the same card: the trial is refused at once.
# packs: free-tier-and-trial, card-and-payments, messaging
# enforce
